Bottomline catch blocks should not see any Program Order violation in the same thread. 

Synchronous Exceptions:
======================
Not sure how JVMs implement it efficiently but if it was me I would make sure the catch handlers for that thread
are assumed to be stuck after every instruction and only do those reorderings that would not be visible to code 
in the catch handler.

Of course if you can prove an instruction cannot throw then go ahead with your reorderings.

Asynchronous Exceptions:
=======================
They are polled until a safe point is reached beyond which reorderings are not visible. 
